From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:31:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Match :target in SVG stacks loaded with a URL fragment

An SVG stack hides every icon with `svg>[id]{display:none}` and shows
the one the URL fragment names with `svg>[id]:target{display:inline}`.
usvg has no document URL, so the `:target` rule was dropped and every
icon stayed hidden. tldraw draws all its toolbar and style-panel icons
as `mask: url(sprite.svg#icon)`, which painted as empty grey squares.

Rewrite `:target` in the sprite's <style> to the id the fragment names
before the parse. CSS images now pass their URL fragment to the image
handler as <img> already did.
